questions.stem:
NIIRA 2025’s mandatory claims settlement timeline provisions represent a fundamental shift in the relationship between Nigerian life insurers and their policyholders. Critically evaluate the impact of these provisions on:
(a) the operational design and technology infrastructure of the life insurance claims function;
(b) the tension between the mandatory settlement timeline and the insurer’s obligation to investigate potentially fraudulent claims;
(c) the adequacy of NAICOM’s enforcement powers to ensure effective compliance; and (d) the long-term market development implications of consistent, industry-wide claims settlement compliance for insurance penetration in Nigeria.
